  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\u03a0$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=\u27e82,3,-1\u27e9+t\u27e8-1,2,3\u27e9,\\,\u03a0:r\\cdot \u27e8-2,1,4\u27e9=11.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e82-t,3+2t,-1+3t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e82-t,3+2t,-1+3t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e8-2,1,4\u27e9 & =11 \\\\ \u27e82-t,3+2t,-1+3t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-2,1,4\u27e9 & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e82-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,5,2\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$",
